      "refersTo": "connection-panel",
      "description": "Strong dark authentication plate over silver light.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-connection\" aria-labelledby=\"ds-connect-title\"><h2 id=\"ds-connect-title\" class=\"ds-connection-title\">Connect your GitHub</h2><p class=\"ds-connection-copy\">One connection. Your real repositories.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-connection{padding:30px;border-radius:20px;box-shadow:0 25px 90px #0007;background:rgba(14,14,14,.79);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.13);backdrop-filter:blur(22px);-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(22px);color:#f2f2f2}.ds-connection-title{font-family:'Sora Variable',sans-serif;font-size:23px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.025em;line-height:1.3;margin:0}.ds-connection-copy{font-family:'DM Sans Variable',sans-serif;color:#bbb;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;margin:10px 0 0}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-connection{padding:27px;border-radius:17px}}@supports not (backdrop-filter:blur(1px)){.ds-connection{background:#151515}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "File View Controls",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "file-view-button",
      "description": "Ordinary grouped view buttons with accurate pressed state.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-file-views\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"File view\"><button class=\"ds-file-view\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Preview</button><button class=\"ds-file-view\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Edit source</button><button class=\"ds-file-view\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Original</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-file-views{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;padding:10px 13px;border-bottom:1px solid #323232}.ds-file-view{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;background:transparent;border:0;padding:6px 9px;border-radius:5px;font-family:'DM Sans Variable',sans-serif;font-size:12px;color:#acacac;cursor:pointer}.ds-file-view[aria-pressed='true']{background:#303030;color:#dddddd}.ds-file-view:hover{color:#e0e0e0}.ds-file-view:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #fff;outline-offset:4px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Project Intelligence",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "project-intelligence",
      "description": "Source-cited project facts on charcoal, with scope disclosure and accurate request usage. Uses native details during review; model requests remain explicit.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-intelligence\" aria-labelledby=\"ds-intelligence-title\"><h2 id=\"ds-intelligence-title\">Understand it. Then improve it.</h2><p>Source-aware analysis, useful documentation, and answers about your code.</p><details><summary>Source evidence</summary><a href=\"#example-source\">sampled/path.ts</a></details></section>",
      "css": ".ds-intelligence{background:#101010e8;border:1px solid #ffffff20;border-radius:16px;padding:26px;color:#c8c8c8;font-family:\"DM Sans Variable\",sans-serif}.ds-intelligence h2{font-family:\"Sora Variable\",sans-serif;font-weight:500;font-size:23px;line-height:1.4;letter-spacing:-.035em}.ds-intelligence p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.85;max-width:75ch}.ds-intelligence summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:12px}.ds-intelligence a{font-size:12px;color:#ccc;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}.ds-intelligence a:focus-visible,.ds-intelligence summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #fff;outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-intelligence{padding:21px}.ds-intelligence h2{font-size:21px}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Photographic darkroom optical bench",
    "overview": "Neutral black grounds a workspace of silver light, frosted charcoal plates, and white controls. The native WebGL lens supplies the optical character; precise typography and quiet borders keep repository work readable over it. This records the user's approved black-and-white replacement and the finished implementation.\n\nGlass carries the connection, navigation, library, and supporting workbench regions. Source and original-file content have opaque dark grounds. Motion belongs to the background and loading feedback; working content stays stable.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Neutral black, white ink, and grayscale state treatments.",
      "Self-hosted Sora headings and DM Sans interface text.",
      "Refracted silver WebGL light behind restrained glass plates.",
      "Opaque source editing and responsive repository review.",
      "Pausable motion, reduced-motion handling, and static visual fallback."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Monochrome State Rule",
        "body": "Keep states achromatic and retain labels, icons, native controls, and borders so hue is never required to understand selection, failure, or completion.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Plate Rule",
        "body": "Keep glass on surrounding controls and containers while source and original-file content use the opaque Source Black ground.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep black, white, and grayscale across controls, states, account images, and the silver lens.",
      "Do use self-hosted Sora for headings, DM Sans for interface text, and Consolas for source content.",
      "Do keep source and original-file content opaque while surrounding regions use glass.",
      "Do retain named controls, visible focus, readable mobile task labels, and 16px mobile text-entry fields.",
      "Do preserve pause, reduced motion, bounded WebGL rendering, and static fallback behavior."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't restore the replaced violet accents or introduce colored state cues.",
      "Don't make visual effects necessary for any repository operation.",
      "Don't communicate selection or completion through tone alone; retain text, icons, and native control states.",
      "Don't turn static metadata tags or entire repository cards into unlabeled controls.",
      "Don't present an in-memory draft as a durable saved artifact or show publish success before a server result."
    ]
  }
}
